Subject: [PATCH] ffmpeg: stop at the first decoder that opens

The probe loop never breaks, so a hardware decoder that opened at try 3
is thrown away at try 4, which unconditionally replaces it with software
h264/hevc and allocates a second context over the first. Try 5 then
reopens the same software decoder a third time. The result is that the
ffmpeg backend always decodes in software - h264_v4l2m2m can never win -
and two AVCodecContexts leak per init.

diff --git a/src/video/ffmpeg.c b/src/video/ffmpeg.c
--- a/src/video/ffmpeg.c
+++ b/src/video/ffmpeg.c
@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@
       avcodec_free_context(&decoder_ctx);
       continue;
     }
+
+    break;
   }
 
   if (decoder == NULL) {
